<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:59:14Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>French presidential hopeful Mélenchon set to launch campaign by vowing to lower retirement age</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67d033d6a83c9749927f11d29e5f644f81eac660dd09734094feab8e2ece5389</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:44:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-french-presidential-hopeful-m_lenchon-launches-campaign-by-vowing-lower-retirement-age--b95f6b426650.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-french-presidential-hopeful-m%C3%A9lenchon-launches-campaign-by-vowing-lower-retirement-age" /><summary type="html">Veteran leftist Jean-Luc Mélenchon is set to formally announce his plan to raise France's minimum wage, cap prices for essential foods and restore the country's retirement age to 60 in a speech launching his 2027 presidential election programme on Saturday. Polls currently indicate that he is the left wing's strongest contender against far-right candidate Marine Le Pen.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France braces for more nationwide protests as Yellow Vests urge 'mass disobedience'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cffcc6c002d4563f6b0cd5f6026fb3be3f5adaaee6f3c64d75d8e92fb439398b</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T13:29:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-more-nationwide-protests-as-yellow-vests-urge-mass-disobedience--294946423bc1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-braces-for-more-nationwide-protests-as-yellow-vests-urge-mass-disobedience" /><summary type="html">French unions and student groups are set to take to the streets for another day of protests on Saturday, while the Yellow Vests movement plans a separate rally in central Paris despite a ban by authorities. The demonstrations follow weeks of youth-led unrest and nationwide strikes that drew hundreds of thousands of workers protesting over the rising cost of living. Paul Smith, Associate Professor in French history and politics at the University of Nottingham, and James André, France 24 reporter at Place de la République, share further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nations League: Zinedine Zidane balances surprise and continuity in his second roster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:094511272b9b4c49a16432654bd19003a5071115000fa3f39340e2de519536aa</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T13:27:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nations-league-zinedine-zidane-balances-surprise-and-continuity-in-his-second-roster--59f0dc28329b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nations-league-zinedine-zidane-balances-surprise-and-continuity-in-his-second-roster" /><summary type="html">Zinedine Zidane has unveiled his France squad for the upcoming Nations League clashes against Italy and Turkey. Pablo Pagis earns a surprise first call-up, while Kylian Mbappé and several other key players return from injury</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Banking scandal topples Paraguay leader</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a30905da8fe58b2b4ac050b815d43c9b85676da3eeeab20bcb3297cbe168f68c</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:16:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/banking-scandal-topples-paraguay-leader--780283ad5424.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/banking-scandal-topples-paraguay-leader" /><summary type="html">Paraguay’s ousted president Santiago Peña has been placed under house arrest after senators unanimously voted to remove him over a banking scandal. The collapse of Ueno Bank left nearly three million customers unable to access their savings. Peña denies any wrongdoing, while his successor, Pedro Alliana, has pledged to compensate those affected.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia launches massive strike on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81a50d024bedc777e31917c25078079158a3f7fd289ff10eedaefd71d86e1595</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:15:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261107-russia-launches-massive-strike-on-kyiv-1--1213cd3ff896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261107-russia-launches-massive-strike-on-kyiv-1" /><summary type="html">As Ukraine prepares for another round of talks with Russia and the United States next week, Moscow has launched a massive overnight strike. At least five people were injured in Kyiv, where Russian missiles damaged residential and commercial buildings, forced the closure of a bridge over the Dnipro River and caused fresh power and water outages. Ophélie Jacobson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Stephen Miller named White House Chief of Staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b36d1abb9e510f9255441ab85713077b595985f4b760df30c9b7373c52ce80e</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:14:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/stephen-miller-named-white-house-chief-of-staff--7469c4aafa30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/stephen-miller-named-white-house-chief-of-staff" /><summary type="html">Following historic Republican losses in the midterm elections, Donald Trump has replaced his chief of staff, Susie Wiles, with her deputy Stephen Miller, the architect of his administration’s immigration crackdown. Wiles had been seen by some as a stabilising force in the White House, but with Democrats now controlling both chambers of Congress, Trump is reportedly seeking a more aggressive approach to pushing his agenda. Caroline Baum reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel coalition talks gain momentum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98e0f2c29047a246aa46488bbe182a3536464f8c158aaa95ff75050c42636b71</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-coalition-talks-gain-momentum--e112145ab913.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-coalition-talks-gain-momentum" /><summary type="html">Following inconclusive elections in Israel, opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot says he is confident of securing the mandate to form a government, as President Isaac Herzog prepares to nominate the first candidate. Eisenkot claims he is making progress in efforts to oust long-serving Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenyan cult leader sentenced to 200 years in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3aced97ac8df6304304bcf9fff8b33968aa798acce13626ff3106e72dcd60f54</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:10:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison-1--17cc7592b605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison-1" /><summary type="html">Kenyan cult leader Paul Mackenzie has been sentenced to 200 years in prison for the deaths of 190 children who were starved to death on his orders in Shakahola Forest. Prosecutors said he had convinced followers to fast to reach heaven before the apocalypse, with some victims beaten, buried alive or dumped in latrines. Twenty-eight accomplices have also been jailed. The case has raised serious questions about the authorities' failure to act on repeated warning signs dating back to 2017, with the death toll from the wider investigation reaching 448 confirmed bodies and around 500 suspected victims.</summary></entry><entry><title>Retired tennis star Gaël Monfils named captain of France's Davis Cup team</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53436f96ef46e8c013aaadae0894b6db8239fc0746c442ea45631da937c13e84</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:07:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-retired-tennis-star-ga_l-monfils-named-captain-of-france-s-davis-cup-team--90c453f0afbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-retired-tennis-star-ga%C3%ABl-monfils-named-captain-of-france-s-davis-cup-team" /><summary type="html">Recently retired tennis player Gaël Monfils was named captain of the French Davis Cup team, the country's tennis federation announced Saturday. France will next take part in the Davis Cup in February 2027 after having failed to qualify for this year's finals in Bologna.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>French presidential election: How far-left Mélenchon became a Gen Z favourite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac2d02c9e0a04cc9f62667ce1f604ad55c0cafa44b744ffae0a15108212e2bd2</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T10:44:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-french-2027-presidential-elections-how-m%C3%A9lenchon-became-a-gen-z-favourite" /><summary type="html">Far-left presidential candidate Jean-Luc Mélenchon presents his policy platform at a key rally near Paris on Saturday. A polarising figure for the general electorate, he is nonetheless beloved among France's youth, who are drawn to his progressive policy proposals and say he empowers them to get more involved in politics.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Pope urges healthcare for all in Uruguay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f84fe7e68700b48680c3686d86ae0be16d9f1d4155b7d3d90ed999cf25a0248</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:41:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pope-urges-healthcare-for-all-in-uruguay--cc244f5a7f44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-urges-healthcare-for-all-in-uruguay" /><summary type="html">Three weeks after undergoing surgery for lung cancer, Pope Francis has begun a three-nation tour of Latin America, saying he felt better than he looked. His first stop is Uruguay, the continent’s most secular country. Jack Pownall reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI Data centres face growing backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e2331be5c9bf774f5bc8a142ca584b2b6f1c6dec4ef60f9583e1418f4cf9ab9</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:39:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ai-data-centres-face-growing-backlash--009b8f3b4c3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ai-data-centres-face-growing-backlash" /><summary type="html">Democrats are also calling for tighter regulation of AI data centres, a concern shared across Europe. In Amsterdam, several hundred activists occupied the site of a planned Microsoft data centre as part of a two-day protest taking place across the continent. Jennie Shin reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: 30 dead in strikes on Taiz market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c907417c557640401f1b6d7c60c17119f6ee5de33a934e559e66e9d5283275e2</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:58:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:37:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-30-dead-in-strikes-on-taiz-market--556471887193.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-30-dead-in-strikes-on-taiz-market" /><summary type="html">At least 30 people have reportedly been killed in an attack on a market in Yemen’s Taiz province, with Houthi rebels blaming Saudi airstrikes. Government forces and local authorities have disputed the claim, instead accusing the Houthis of indiscriminate fire. The province has witnessed intense clashes in recent weeks and is home to around half of the more than 300,000 people displaced by the latest fighting. Caroline Baum reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>USA: Democrats vow to investigate Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9866d2604e673ca20af23a6013e12977f1732244196b7a830793b73d2649b8e2</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:36:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/usa-democrats-vow-to-investigate-donald-trump--9175a9d654b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/usa-democrats-vow-to-investigate-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">In this new era of divided government, Democratic lawmakers say their priorities will be tackling the rising cost of living, investigating alleged corruption and tightening oversight of ICE agents. Antonia Kerrigan reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Fresh demonstration kicks off in Paris as France’s Yellow Vests urge 'mass disobedience'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4f79a00f96468921450c9f241cc8c9242099e8681fd948431554488640da346</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:59:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T08:17:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-live-france-braces-for-more-nationwide-protests-as-yellow-vests-urge-mass-disobedience--85f01cbeffa8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261107-live-france-braces-for-more-nationwide-protests-as-yellow-vests-urge-mass-disobedience" /><summary type="html">French unions and student groups took to the streets for another day of protests on Saturday, while the Yellow Vests movement planned a separate rally in central Paris despite a ban by authorities. The demonstrations follow weeks of youth-led unrest and nationwide strikes that drew hundreds of thousands of workers protesting over the rising cost of living. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Russia hits Kyiv and surrounding region in massive overnight strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e21c7825aa7a2f652e24ecb0b74f5d186cc423a50dbdfa71ce029aeb30aeb437</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:59:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T08:08:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-moscow-strikes-kyiv-as-ukraine-prepares-for-talks-with-russia-and-the-us--a1d6ff529852.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-moscow-strikes-kyiv-as-ukraine-prepares-for-talks-with-russia-and-the-us" /><summary type="html">Moscow ⁠carried out missile ​and drone attacks on Kyiv and the surrounding region overnight Friday to Saturday, targeting energy infrastructure and killing at least one person while wounding eight, authorities said. Russia recently stepped up air strikes on ​Ukraine, worsening living conditions for residents who have limited access to power and water.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Paraguay places ousted president Peña under house arrest after bank collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1e7c45fb053fa6fd576835416e6565fb4f16a6213d35e480f6f24a40d21a4d4</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:59:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T06:18:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-ousted-paraguay-president-under-house-arrest-after-banking-crisis--da227b173e79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-ousted-paraguay-president-under-house-arrest-after-banking-crisis" /><summary type="html">Paraguayan authorities placed ousted president Santiago Peña under house arrest on Friday, shortly after the Senate unanimously removed him from office over a massive banking crisis that locked nearly half of Paraguayans out of their savings. Peña offered his resignation over the scandal, but lawmakers pressed ahead with impeachment proceedings that stripped him of political immunity.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Giant pandas loaned by China make their public debut at US zoo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce8658cda50228985011e87f00847bbb5b3d4b981747de569ae282736f68f7f7</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:59:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T02:45:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-giant-pandas-loaned-by-china-make-public-debut-at-us-zoo--998a66c6893a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-giant-pandas-loaned-by-china-make-public-debut-at-us-zoo" /><summary type="html">Zoo-goers watched two giant pandas loaned by China make their public debut Friday in Atlanta, where they will be hosted for the next 10 years. The pair joins the many pandas shipped to zoos around the world as part of Beijing's "panda diplomacy" program aimed at cultivating foreign ties.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Kenyan cult leader sentenced to 200 years in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be2390792983b7ed47aa8c247e681028aaaa119c89c5fc0515d9560fc270ce73</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T21:23:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison--479d3d59e388.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenyan-cult-leader-sentenced-to-200-years-in-prison" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, cult leader Paul Mackenzie is sentenced to 200 years in prison for the murder of 190 children starved ‌to death on his orders. Also, in South Africa, activists warn that new data centres could put added pressure on already strained water and electricity supplies. And Senegal continues to celebrate the spirit of sport at the Youth Olympic Games.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Europe bomb hoaxes widen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a49a239135561107e7bd839ffe741b6dd29b9a7da63c7c24705b30253caa2c6e</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T21:22:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-bomb-hoaxes-widen--730544f3c51f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-bomb-hoaxes-widen" /><summary type="html">The series of hoax bomb scares sent to several Irish media outlets and European airlines are likely part of a coordinated campaign of disruption, according to the Irish government. Dozens of commercial flights have been targetted by email with threats said to be over and above the typical hoax in specificty. Ireland's broadcaster RTE who's staff evacuated the premises this morning and several Italian airlines, say they received a mesage cliaming to be from a Russian extremist group calling itself the Fighters of the Male State, which denied its implication. France 24's Jean-Emile Jammine speaks to Eric Schouten, founder and CEO of Dyami Security Intelligence.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo calls for healthcare to be 'accessible for all' during Uruguay visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a32f4b358001da11d6dd4022fd7cafdbb4328a2cda86716768f8cce3ccc3a879</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T21:14:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-pope-leo-arrives-in-uruguay-for-first-stop-on-12-day-south-america-tour--c31bc7a85d30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-pope-leo-arrives-in-uruguay-for-first-stop-on-12-day-south-america-tour" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV on Friday called for healthcare to be "accessible to all" as he began a visit to Uruguay just three weeks after having undergone lung surgery. The 12-day tour of South America, which will also include stops in Argentina and Peru, is seen as something of a homecoming for the pontiff, who lived in Peru for almost two decades and holds joint US and Peruvian citizenship.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump announces immigration hardliner Stephen Miller as new chief of staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c9c0bcdd329e4a21ba49cc36fb485a624921753fb2f4d235e37e5b1b10d5422</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T20:51:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-announces-immigration-hardliner-stephen-miller-as-new-chief-of-staff--0db36603c7f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-announces-immigration-hardliner-stephen-miller-as-new-chief-of-staff" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Friday said advisor Stephen Miller would become his new chief of staff. Miller has been instrumental in driving the Trump administration's mass deportation programme and faced particular criticism after the deadly shootings of two Minneapolis protesters by ICE agents in January.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Midterms: A Maga PostMortem, Europe’s ‘Shape Shifting’ Protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62ae18078b0cee4bd5b524acfd92b684c2e79b665232faad4ab6b34326408689</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T20:08:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261106-midterms-a-maga-postmortem-europe-s-shape-shifting-protests--b53f797a61ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261106-midterms-a-maga-postmortem-europe-s-shape-shifting-protests" /><summary type="html">A World This Week ‘Mid Terms Special’ 
 
Gavin Lee is joined by panel of four distinguished international correspondents to assess the aftermath of the worst Republican election result since the 1970s, post Watergate. We ask, is peak MAGA over? What will now change at home and abroad? And who ends the week in pole position as Presidential frontrunner for 2028?
 
We also consider the scale and scope of Europe Wide Protests:  
 
This week housing organisations, trade unions and activist groups from seven countries met in Paris issuing a joint call for demonstrations. Are the national protest movements becoming a coordinated European movement?</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>A homegrown Georgia moderate and pragmatist: Is Senator Ossoff the future of the Democratic Party?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03b64a90b9a3a56940a0c69e4e54decb02a853bdd7a82bd3f7578fd0b57a74cd</id><updated>2026-11-07T14:57:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T19:49:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-a-homegrown-georgia-moderate-and-pragmatist-is-senator-ossoff-the-future-of-the-democratic---71311042af65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-a-homegrown-georgia-moderate-and-pragmatist-is-senator-ossoff-the-future-of-the-democratic-party" /><summary type="html">Is Senator Jon Ossoff the future of the Democratic Party? Following a resounding midterm victory in Georgia, a former Republican stronghold, the 39-year-old senator has emerged as a prominent figure as the Democrats look ahead to 2028 for their next presidential nominee. His natural confidence, polished media performances and ability to appeal to a diverse electorate have prompted comparisons with Barack Obama. Yet behind the excitement surrounding his national prospects lies a more complicated question: whether political momentum in the Senate necessarily translates into a presidential frontrunner.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry></feed>
